// Auto-generated plain-text knowledge base from the Help Center articles.
// Used to ground Gemini's answers in the site's real content.
const KNOWLEDGE_BASE = `
### Getting started on Nexor Sparks (id: getting-started)
Welcome to Nexor Sparks. Follow the steps below to create a new account and set up your profile. Create an account: open the app or website and tap the Sign Up tab. Enter your email or phone number, a unique username, and a strong password. Confirm your email/phone with the verification code. Enter your age accurately — you must meet the minimum age policy to use Nexor Sparks. Complete your profile: add a clear profile photo and a short bio. Follow people based on your interests so your feed gets personalized. Adjust your notification and privacy settings to your liking. After logging in for the first time, we recommend reading the Privacy Policy and Community Guidelines at least once.

### Forgot your password? How to reset it (id: password-forgot)
If you've forgotten your password, don't worry — you can get back into your account in a few steps. Steps to reset your password: tap "Forgot Password?" on the login screen. Enter your registered email or phone number. You'll be sent a verification code or reset link — open it. Set a new, strong password (use a mix of letters, numbers, and symbols). Log in again with your new password. If you're not receiving the reset code: check your spam/junk folder. Confirm you entered the same email/number linked to your account. Wait a few minutes and try again. After resetting your password, if you think someone else may have had access to your account, be sure to read the Hacked Account guide.

### Your account has been hacked or compromised (id: hacked-account)
If you think someone else has accessed your account, immediately follow the steps below. Signs of compromise: Pulses or messages are going out from your account that you didn't post. Your profile info (bio, photo, email, password) has changed on its own. You received a login/password change notification that you didn't make yourself. You're unable to log into your own account. What to do immediately: Change your password right away — if you can still log in, follow the "Password Reset" guide to set a new, strong, and unique password. If you can't log in — use the "Forgot Password" reset link to regain access. Check active sessions — go to settings and check whether any unknown device is logged in, and log them out. Verify your connected email/phone — confirm the recovery email/number is really yours. Review recent activity — delete/undo any unauthorized Pulse, message, or profile change. If you can't reset your password because the attacker has also changed your recovery email/phone, submit an account recovery request via the AI Assistant (bottom right corner) or the "Report a Problem" page. Tips to keep your account safe in the future: use a unique password everywhere — never repeat the same password on another website. Never enter your password on unfamiliar links or messages (avoid phishing). Keep checking your login activity regularly.

### Deactivating or deleting your account (id: delete-account)
You can either temporarily deactivate or permanently delete your account. Deactivate (temporary): when you deactivate, your profile, Pulses, and messages are all hidden, but no data is deleted. Everything becomes active again as soon as you log back in. Delete (permanent): permanently deleting removes your profile, Pulses, articles, messages, and data forever. This action cannot be undone, so save/download any important data first if needed. Go to the Account section in Settings. Choose the Deactivate or Delete Account option. Enter your password to confirm. If you just want a break, it's better to use Deactivate instead of Delete.

### Posting Pulses and Articles (id: pulses-articles)
On Nexor Sparks, you can share your moments as Pulses, or write longer content in the Articles format. Posting a Pulse: create your Pulse by adding a photo, text, or media. Be sure to preview it before posting. You can edit or delete it even after posting. Editing/deleting your content: go to your Pulse/Article and tap the (⋯) menu. Choose Edit or Delete. Once deleted, content cannot be restored. Keep in mind while posting content: every Pulse and Article must follow our Community Guidelines. Content that violates the guidelines may be removed.

### What is the "AI" label on AI-generated content (id: ai-content-label)
When content has been fully or significantly generated or edited with AI tools, you may see a golden "AI" label on it. Why this label matters: it keeps the community transparent about how content was made. It builds trust — people know whether content is a real photo/video or AI-generated. Labeling your own AI-generated content: if you're creating content with AI tools, label it honestly when posting. Posting misleading AI content without a label is considered a violation of the Community Guidelines.

### Verified badge and Organization badge (id: verification)
Nexor Sparks has two types of badges that appear next to a profile's name. Verified Badge: this badge confirms that the account is authentic and its identity has been verified. It helps distinguish real users from spam/fake accounts. Organization Badge: this badge appears separately alongside the verified badge and confirms that the account belongs to an official organization/brand. Badges only indicate authenticity — they don't imply any kind of endorsement or priority. Beware of fake verified badges: if an account claims to be verified but doesn't have the real badge, report it via the "Report a Problem" page.

### Privacy Policy (id: privacy-policy)
This Privacy Policy explains how Nexor Sparks collects, uses, stores, and protects your information. What we collect: Account info: username, email/phone, password (encrypted), profile details. Content: your Pulses, articles, messages, comments. Usage data: how you use the app, device and log information. How we use it: to provide and personalize app services for you. For account safety and fraud prevention. To improve the app and fix bugs. Data sharing: we do not sell your personal data to third parties without consent. Data is only shared when legally required, or with service providers (like hosting) who work on our behalf. Your rights: the right to access, correct, or delete your data. The right to deactivate/delete your account at any time. Control who can see your content via privacy settings. Data retention: we retain data as long as your account is active. When you delete your account, data is deleted or anonymized in accordance with applicable law. For any privacy-related questions, talk to the AI Assistant or use the "Report a Problem" page.

### Terms of Service (id: terms-of-service)
By using Nexor Sparks, you agree to these Terms of Service. Eligibility: you must meet the minimum age requirement to use this app and must provide accurate information. Your responsibility: you are responsible for the security of your account and password. You are responsible for the accuracy and legality of the content you post. Creating multiple fake or impersonation accounts is not allowed. Content ownership: you remain the owner of the content you create. By posting, you grant Nexor Sparks only enough license to display and distribute the content on the app. Prohibited conduct: harassment, hate speech, spam, fraud, illegal content, and intellectual property violations are strictly prohibited — see Community Guidelines for details. Suspension and termination: repeated or serious violations of the Terms or Community Guidelines may result in account suspension or termination. Changes to Terms: we may update these Terms from time to time. Major changes will be communicated through the app.

### Community Guidelines (id: community-guidelines)
Nexor Sparks believes in building a safe, respectful, and authentic community. These guidelines apply to every user. Be authentic: use your real identity — impersonation is not allowed. Honestly label AI-generated content. Fake engagement (bots, bought followers) is not allowed. Be respectful: harassment, bullying, or threats are absolutely not allowed. Hate speech — based on race, religion, gender, sexuality, disability — is not allowed. Violating anyone's privacy (sharing personal info) is not allowed. Post safe content: graphic violence, gore, or disturbing content is not allowed. Nudity or sexually explicit content is not allowed. Content promoting self-harm is not allowed — if you're struggling, please talk to a trusted person or a local helpline right away. Promoting illegal activities (drugs, weapons, fraud) is not allowed. Spam and misinformation: repetitive spam, misleading links, and deliberately spreading false information are not allowed. What happens when you violate: content may be removed. A warning may be issued. Repeated or serious violations may result in temporary or permanent account suspension. If you see any content or user breaking the guidelines, report it right away via the "Report a Problem" page.

### Copyright & Intellectual Property Policy (id: copyright-policy)
Nexor Sparks respects others' intellectual property and expects the same from its users. Copyright rules: only post content you own, or that you have permission/license to post. Using others' photos, videos, music, or writing without permission is copyright infringement. If your copyrighted content has been used without permission: you can file a complaint through our dedicated copyright report page. You'll need to submit a link to the infringing content, proof of your ownership, and your contact details. File a Copyright Report. If your content was removed due to a copyright claim: if you believe the removal was a mistake (e.g. the content is your original work), you can submit a counter-request through the same report page. Accounts with repeated copyright violations may be suspended or permanently banned.

### Reporting content, an account, or a problem (id: report-content)
If you find any content, account, or behavior that goes against our Community Guidelines, it's important to report it. Reporting a Pulse/Article: go to the post and tap the (⋯) menu. Select Report. Choose the most relevant reason (spam, harassment, nudity, hate speech, misinformation, etc.). Reporting an account: go to that user's profile. Choose Report Account from the (⋯) menu. State a reason and submit. Reporting an app bug or technical problem: describe the bug, crash, or technical issue to the AI Assistant (bottom right corner) along with a screenshot. Reports stay anonymous — the user you reported won't know who reported them. Emergency or immediate safety threat: if there is an immediate threat to someone's life or safety, contact your local emergency services first.

### Blocking and Safety Tools (id: blocking-safety)
Nexor Sparks gives you several tools to control your experience. Blocking: when you block someone, they won't be able to see your profile, Pulses, or messages, and won't be able to contact you. Open that user's profile. Select Block from the (⋯) menu. Muting: when you mute someone, they can still contact you, but you won't get notifications about their activity — and they won't know you've muted them. Privacy settings: control who can see your profile. Control who can message you. Set restrictions on comments and tags. If someone is harassing you, be sure to report them in addition to blocking them.

`;

// Cloudflare Pages Function — POST /api/chat
// Keeps the Gemini API key on the server. It is NEVER sent to the browser.
// Set GEMINI_API_KEY in: Cloudflare Pages dashboard → your project →
// Settings → Environment variables → Production (and Preview) → Add variable.

const SYSTEM_PROMPT = `You are "Sparky", the AI Help Assistant for Nexor Sparks, a social app where users post "Pulses" (short posts) and "Articles".
Answer briefly (2-5 sentences), in friendly, clear English, like Instagram's help bot.

You must answer ONLY using the information in the HELP CENTER KNOWLEDGE BASE below — this is the site's real, official help content.
Do not invent steps, policies, or features that are not written in the knowledge base.
If the knowledge base does not cover the user's question, say clearly that you don't have that information yet and suggest they use the "Report a Problem" page, instead of guessing.
Never claim to take real actions (like actually resetting a password) — only guide the user on the steps to do it themselves in the app, based on the knowledge base.

===== HELP CENTER KNOWLEDGE BASE =====
${KNOWLEDGE_BASE}
===== END OF KNOWLEDGE BASE =====`;

export async function onRequestPost(context) {
  const { request, env } = context;

  if (!env.GEMINI_API_KEY) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Server misconfigured: missing GEMINI_API_KEY" }), {
      status: 500,
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  }

  let body;
  try {
    body = await request.json();
  } catch {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Invalid request body" }), {
      status: 400,
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  }

  const userMessage = String(body.message || "").slice(0, 1500);
  if (!userMessage.trim()) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Empty message" }), {
      status: 400,
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  }

  try {
    const resp = await fetch(
      "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/gemini-flash-latest:generateContent",
      {
        method: "POST",
        headers: {
          "Content-Type": "application/json",
          "X-goog-api-key": env.GEMINI_API_KEY,
        },
        body: JSON.stringify({
          contents: [
            {
              parts: [{ text: `${SYSTEM_PROMPT}\n\nUser message: ${userMessage}` }],
            },
          ],
        }),
      }
    );

    if (!resp.ok) {
      const errText = await resp.text();
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "AI service error", detail: errText }), {
        status: 502,
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
      });
    }

    const data = await resp.json();
    const reply =
      data?.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts?.[0]?.text?.trim() ||
      "Sorry, I wasn't able to generate a reply right now. Please try rephrasing your question.";

    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ reply }), {
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  } catch (err) {
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ error: "Request failed" }), {
      status: 500,
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
    });
  }
}
